KZ3 patch 1071 (SPU pass 56): SPU extended-range single precision on the lanes the host gets wrong.
The SPU has no single-precision Inf/NaN (exponent 255 is an ordinary binade, overflow saturates, SPU ISA v1.2 s.9.1);
the helpers read such words as host Inf/NaN. fa/fs/fm, fma/fms/fnms (both paths), fceq/fcgt/fcmeq/fcmgt,
cflts/cfltu, csflt/cuflt and fi now recompute a lane exactly when an operand or the host result has exponent 255
(spu__xr_mask: one SSE compare per operand), using the exact lane code of sp00nznet/ps3recomp PR #287 by
NoahBPeterson (spu__sf_pack/split/sum, fa/fm/fma lanes, key compares, cflts lanes, integer fi). All other lanes keep
their current results and rounding. KZ3_SPU_XR=0 keeps the host results (A/B). Host test tools/spu/test_spu_xr.sh.

